<title>RUSSIA: Russia raises rail tariffs 2.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Russia raises rail tariffs 2.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia increased its freight rail charges by 2.5 percent on Friday, adding to the costs oil traders pay to get Russian material to Western markets, a transport official said.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Transport Ministry's press service said the hikes were the result of a government decree calling for measures to regulate prices charged by natural monopolies.</p>
<p>Charges for loading operations rose 2.8 percent.</p>
<p>A ministry press release said a discount of 10 to 30 percent for transport of certain cargoes would be retained.</p>
<p>The tariff increases affect all rail links in Russia and to former Soviet republics, including the Baltics.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
